{{Quote|Welcome to ''Tython'', Lord Vader.|Doctor Chelli Aphra, to Darth Vader|<ref name="Doctor Aphra 40" />}}
'''Tython''' was a terrestrial [[planet]] located in [[Deep Core]]'s [[Tython system]] that played a pivotal role in the history of the [[Jedi Order]]. A verdant world that was incredibly rich in [[the Force]], Tython was eventually abandoned when the ever-changing [[Hyperspace route|hyperlanes]] in the region drifted away from the planet and became shrouded in myth. The [[Martyrium of Frozen Tears]] was built by [[Jedi]] there, and some Jedi [[scholar]]s made the case that Tython was the site of the Jedi Order's [[First Jedi Temple|first temple]]. During the [[Galactic Civil War]], [[Doctor]] [[Chelli Lona Aphra]] led the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Commander-in-Chief|commander]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] to Tython's [[Meridional Ice Cap]] to mislead him as to the location of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance's]] [[Echo Base|main base]], which was actually on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] planet [[Hoth]].

==Description==
Tython was a verdant,<ref name="Falcon 36">{{BuildFalconCite|36|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref>uninhabited,<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" /> terrestrial [[planet]]<ref name="Doctor Aphra 40" /> located in the [[Tython system]]<ref name="Falcon 36" /> in [[the galaxy]]'s [[Deep Core]], positioned at the coordinates K-10 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="Appendix" /> It was orbited by at least two [[moon]]s, with the primary being known as [[Ashla (moon)|Ashla]],<ref name="Rising Storm" /> and was incredibly rich in [[the Force]].<ref name="Falcon 36" /> Areas on its surface included the [[Meridional Ice Cap]],<ref name="Doctor Aphra 40" /> and a more [[Temperature|temperate]] [[Unidentified temperate region|region]].<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" /> Tython was home to a number of native fauna, including beasts,<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> [[bird]]s,<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" /> [[Butterfly|butterflies]],<ref name="Chapter 14" /> and small [[mammal]]s. Tython was covered in [[forest]]s, [[grass]]lands,<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" /> and [[mountain]]s.<ref name="Chapter 14" />

It shared its name with [[Tythonian pendant]]s,<ref name="THR 1">[[The High Republic (2021) 1|''The High Republic'' (2021) 1]]</ref> [[Tythonian Mastery Token]]s,<ref name="Rising Storm" /> and [[Jedha City]]'s [[Tythoni Square]].<ref name="R1 UVG">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref>

==History==
===Early history===
[[File:MartyriumFrozenTears-2016DoctorAphra40.jpg|thumb|250px|left|The ancient Jedi built the Martyrium of Frozen Tears.]]
Tython played a pivotal role in the history of the [[Jedi Order]].<ref name="Falcon 36" /> The [[sacred Jedi texts]] contained a description of Tython's notable beasts.<ref name="TROS VD" /> In ancient times, the Jedi built the [[Martyrium of Frozen Tears]] in the Meridional Ice Cap.<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" /> Tython was eventually abandoned when the ever-changing [[Hyperspace route|hyperlanes]] in the region drifted away from the planet.<ref name="Falcon 36" /> 

Shrouded in myth, some [[Jedi]] [[scholar]]s made the case that Tython was the location of the Jedi Order's [[First Jedi Temple|first temple]],<ref name="CL" /> although in reality, it was located on the planet [[Ahch-To]].<ref name="Episode VIII">{{Film|VIII}}</ref> The fabled planet was thought to have troves of [[holocron]]s and [[datacard]]s filled with Jedi wisdom from throughout the ages, and if one were to discover it, they could gain access to unmatched power.<ref name="Nexus of Power">''[[Nexus of Power]]''</ref>

===High Republic Era===
The ancient [[Ga'Garen Codex]] held in the [[Jedi Archives]] mentioned the planet Tython and its primary moon, Ashla. Its mysteries had confounded [[linguist]]s for a long [[time]].<ref name="The Rising Storm">''[[The High Republic: The Rising Storm]]''</ref>
Months after the [[Dedication of the Starlight Beacon|dedication]] of the [[Starlight Beacon]]<ref name="The Rising Storm" /> in [[232 BBY]],<ref name="High Republic Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars: The High Republic Character Encyclopedia]]''</ref> [[Jedi Master]] [[Elzar Mann]] consulted the Ga'Garen Codex and journeyed aboard his [[Jedi Vector]] to the [[Isle of Seclusion]] on Ashla. Mann had experienced a terrible [[Force vision]] during the aforementioned dedication, and chose the Isle as a place where he could [[Meditation|meditate]] in solitude on what he had seen. He waded into the ocean surrounding the Isle, and eventually received a vision that directed him to the planet [[Valo]].<ref name="The Rising Storm" /> Jedi Master [[Harli Cogra]] mentioned Elzar Mann's mission to Ashla, in ''[[Chronicles of the Jedi]]'', a document detailing the Jedi of the High Republic written in the [[Standard week|weeks]] following the [[destruction of Starlight Beacon]]<ref name="Chronicles of the Jedi">''[[Star Wars: The High Republic: Chronicles of the Jedi]]''</ref> in [[230 BBY]].<ref name="High Republic Character Encyclopedia" />

===Imperial Era===
{{Quote|And dad was ''right'' for once, ''huh''? A martyrium from the earliest ''Jedi cults'', right in the ''Deep Core''.|Doctor Chelli Aphra, to 0-0-0|<ref name="Doctor Aphra 40" />}}
[[File:MeridionalIceCap-2016DoctorAphra40.jpg|thumb|250px|right|The Meridional Ice Cap.]]
During the [[Imperial Era]], the [[15th Deep Core Reserve Fleet]] operated a [[hyperspace]] interdiction checkpoint along the only known hyperspace route between the [[Empress Teta system]] and the interior of the Deep Core.<ref name="Nexus of Power" />

In [[3 ABY]],<ref name="Aphra 40 date">{{Aphra2016Date|40}}</ref> in an attempt to save her loved ones who were located at the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance's]] [[Echo Base|headquarters]] on [[Hoth]], [[Doctor]] [[Chelli Lona Aphra]] brought [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Imperial Military|forces]] led by [[Galactic Emperor|Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine's]] [[Emperor's Fist|lieutenant]], [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]], to Tython, distracting them from discovering the location of the rebel base. Aphra took Vader to the Martyrium of Frozen Tears in the Meridional Ice Cap on Tython, where the the [[Dark Lord of the Sith|Dark Lord]] and his subordinates were ambushed.<ref name="Doctor Aphra 40" />

At some point between 3 ABY and [[4 ABY]],<ref name="SW19 Date">[[Star Wars (2020) 19|''Star Wars'' (2020) 19]] takes place in between {{Film|V}} and {{Film|VI}}, which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[3 ABY]] and [[4 ABY]], respectively.</ref> the rebel and aspiring Jedi [[Luke Skywalker]] had acquired an [[Aurebesh]] list of possible Jedi locations from the Galactic Empire, whom he assumed had destroyed and ransacked all of them. The list included Tython.<ref name="SW19">[[Star Wars (2020) 19|''Star Wars'' (2020) 19]]</ref>

===New Republic Era===
{{Quote|This is Tython. That's where we're gonna try to find you a Jedi.|Din Djarin, to Grogu|<ref name="Chapter 14" />}}
[[File:GroguMeditating-TMCh14.png|thumb|left|250px|Grogu meditating upon the seeing stone at the temple.]]
In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{MandoDate|14}}</ref> the former Jedi [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] instructed the [[Mandalorian]] [[Din Djarin]] to take the [[Force-sensitive]] [[Youngling|child]] [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] to Tython.<ref name="Chapter 13">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 13: The Jedi}}</ref> Djarin did so, traveling to Tython and placing Grogu on the [[seeing stone]]. Grogu entered a meditative state while perched on the stone. Meanwhile, the [[bounty hunter]] [[Boba Fett]], along with his partner, [[Fennec Shand]], in his ship, ''[[Slave I]]'', tracked Djarin to Tython, intent on reacquiring [[Boba Fett's armor|his armor]]<ref name="Chapter 14" /> that Djarin got from [[Cobb Vanth]] on [[Tatooine]].<ref name="Chapter 9">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 9: The Marshal}}</ref> They were [[Battle of Tython (9 ABY)|attacked]] by [[Moff]] [[Gideon]]'s [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|Imperial forces]], and after a skirmish and the destruction of Djarin's ship, the ''[[Razor Crest]]'', the [[foundling]] was ultimately abducted by the [[warlord]]'s [[Phase-III Dark Trooper|dark troopers]].<ref name="Chapter 14" />

In [[21 ABY]],<ref name="Shadow date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[Shadow of the Sith]]'' to [[21 ABY]].</ref> Jedi Master Luke Skywalker traveled to Tython and meditate upon the seeing stone. There, he had a vision of him on [[Exegol]] where he [[Lightsaber combat|dueled]] nine wraiths before the [[Force spirit]] of his [[Parent|father]], Anakin Skywalker, came to his aid.<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" />

==Locations==
{{Quote|Go to the planet Tython. There you will find the ancient ruins of a temple that has a strong connection to the Force.|Ahsoka Tano, to Din Djarin|<ref name="Chapter 13" />}}
[[File:Tython-2016DoctorAphra40.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Vader's forces gather over Tython.]]
A Tythonian mountain was the site of an ancient [[Force-henge|temple]] that had a strong connection to the Force, though it had fallen into ruin by 9 ABY. At the top of the mountain was a seeing stone.<ref name="Chapter 13" />

The Meridional Ice Cap contained the underground Martyrium of Frozen Tears, which had a Force-sensitive [[confessional]] made of solid [[kyberite]]. The ice cap was also dotted with ancient statues of robed figures near the Martyrium's entrance.<ref name="Doctor Aphra 40" /> The seeing stone was on the top of a hill in a scrubland area.<ref name="Chapter 14" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Luke, you don't even know the "grip of tython" or "the seven moves". You can't&hellip;|Leia Lars|<ref name="Second Draft">''[[Adventures of the Starkiller, Episode I: The Star Wars]]''</ref>}}
The term "tython" originates in the [[Adventures of the Starkiller, Episode I: The Star Wars|second draft]] of what would become [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']].<ref name="Second Draft" /> Tython was first mentioned in the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in ''[[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 36]]'', a [[2015]] magazine for the ''[[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon]]'' series.<ref name="Falcon 36" /> It first appeared in the [[2019]] comic book [[Doctor Aphra (2016) 40|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 40]].<ref name="Doctor Aphra 40" /> In the "[[Chapter 14: The Tragedy]]," the sixth episode of ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]''{{'s}} [[The Mandalorian Season Two|second season]], the filming location of Tython was Rocky Peak Park in Simi Valley, California.<ref name="Disney Gallery">{{DisneyGallery|Disney Gallery: The Mandalorian: Making of Season Two|Making of Season Two}}</ref>

[[File:Tython_forest.jpg|thumb|right|300px|Concept art of Tython for ''Star Wars: The Old Republic'']]
In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, Tython was first mentioned in the [[2002]] sourcebook ''[[Power of the Jedi Sourcebook]]'',<ref name="POTJ">''[[Power of the Jedi Sourcebook]]''</ref> where it was the original homeworld of the [[Je'daii Order]]<ref name="DOTJ 0">[[Star Wars: Dawn of the Jedi 0|''Star Wars: Dawn of the Jedi'' 0]]</ref> and its successor organization, the [[Jedi Order/Legends|Jedi Order]].<ref name="Holonet">{{Holonet|planets|tython|Tython}}</ref>

[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens Beginner Game|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' Beginner Game]] places "Tython" predominantly in Standard Galactic Grid square, L-10 and partially in K-10, as does supporting ''Star Wars'' Legends material.<ref name="TFABG" /> However, new canon maps, starting with the [[Star Wars Galaxy Map (poster)|''Star Wars'' Galaxy Map poster]], placed it instead in grid square K-10,<ref name="Poster">{{GalaxyMapPoster}}</ref> and the [[October 13]], [[2025]]<ref name="Substack 2">{{Substack|subdomain=jasonfry|url=p/star-wars-galaxy-map-update|text=Star Wars Galaxy Map Update|name=[[Jason Fry]]|username=jasonfry|date=2025-10-13}}</ref> iteration of the [[Star Systems of the Galaxy]] appendix of [[star system]]s officially placed Tython in K-10 as well.<ref name="Appendix" />

